        "description": "Requires an existing user_id UUID. Send JSON with body and user_id. Set Local user_id from Create user before sending. Body length must be at most 140 bytes, as checked by Go len(string). Empty body is currently accepted. Space-separated words kerfuffle, sharbert and fornax are replaced by **** case-insensitively. Success: 201 JSON with id, created_at, updated_at, body, user_id. Copy id into Local chirp_id. Invalid JSON/UUID or zero UUID: 400 {\"error\":\"Invalid request\"}; oversized body: 400 {\"error\":\"Chirp is too long\"}; database errors, including nonexistent user: 500 {\"error\":\"something went wrong\"}. Source: main.go createChirp and profaneHandler; sql/queries/chirps.sql.",
